  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 219 AM CDT Wed Jul 1 2026\n\nA large area of high pressure will remain stationed over the eastern \nUS until late this week. Multiple shortwaves will weaken the ridge \nto end the work week, enhancing moisture across South Texas with \nPWATs between 1.7- 2.0\". This moisture and seabreeze will bring \ndaily very low rain chances. Uncertainty returns to the forecast \nthis weekend into next week with some models showing a mid-level \ntrough digging into South Texas or cut-off low entering Mexico while \nothers don't. Regardless which way it shakes out, rain chances will \nremain very low.",
